      "id": "ahmad-al-harthy",
      "wikidata": "Q4695244",
      "summary": {
        "text": "Ahmad Al Harthy (born 31 August 1981 in Muscat, Oman) is an Omani racing driver who currently competes in the FIA World Endurance Championship in the LMGT3 Class in the No. 46 BMW M4 GT3 for BMW M Team WRT alongside nine-time MotoGP Champion Valentino Rossi and ADAC GT Masters champion, two time 24 Hours of Nürburgring winner, and DTM vice champion, Kelvin Van Der Linde. He won the 2012 Porsche Carrera Cup Great Britain Pro-Am 1 Championship and in 2017 became the Blancpain Endurance Cup Pro-Am Champion along with British team-mate Jonny Adam.",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmad_Al_Harthy"
      },
      "birthDate": "2009-08-31",
      "birthPlace": "Mascate, Omán",
